# Architecture preferences (Global)

- Follow the repo’s existing architecture/patterns first.
- If the repo lacks structure: use **simple layering**:
  - UI/handlers (I/O, HTTP, CLI) → service/domain (business logic) → data access (DB/external clients)
- Prefer one-way dependencies; avoid circular imports and “god modules.”
- Validate at boundaries; keep core logic as pure as reasonable.
- Propose larger restructures only when requested or required, and do them incrementally.
- If multiple patterns exist: choose the **most common** unless instructed otherwise.
